infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Same word, two different things
  desc Partitioning scales manageability on one Postgres; sharding scales throughput across many
  compares
    - label Partitioning
      children
        - label One Postgres instance
          desc All partitions share one primary, CPU, RAM
        - label Pruning, not throughput
          desc WHERE on partition key scans only relevant partitions
        - label Instant retention DROP
          desc DROP old partition: no slow DELETE, no VACUUM bloat
        - label Joins stay free
          desc Everything co-located on one machine
        - label Since PostgreSQL 10
          desc Declarative PARTITION BY
    - label Sharding
      children
        - label Many Postgres instances
          desc N physically separate primaries, independent IO
        - label ~N× write throughput
          desc Each shard key routes to its own instance
        - label Scales past one machine
          desc Storage and CPU grow with shard count
        - label Cross-shard joins cost
          desc Free only if co-located by the same key
        - label Via Citus or app routing
          desc N× per-shard operational overhead
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
